LevelDB 1.23 (BSD-3-Clause, see upstream LICENSE)
https://github.com/google/leveldb/releases/tag/1.23
The distfile hashes are inherited from pkgsrc. patch-chromium-compat is an
AI-assisted selection from upstream LevelDB through Chromium's pinned commit
7ee830d02b623e8ffe0b95d59a74db1e58da04c5:
https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/leveldb/+/7ee830d02b623e8ffe0b95d59a74db1e58da04c5
It includes correctness fixes for log close failures, compaction, footer bounds,
and pointer arithmetic, plus Chromium-required source compatibility. The
C++17 variable-template spellings are adapted to C++11. The 1.23 public Cache
and Options layouts, internal length-prefixed-slice overload, existing codecs,
and storage format remain unchanged; Zstd additions are not included.
Patch provenance: upstream LevelDB contributors, accepted upstream in the
history above; the selection and C++11 adaptations are local EmberBSD work.
This recipe alone does not establish target runtime or browser acceptance.

Validation: source owner preparation and altered archive/patch rejection pass.
The direct native and amd64 target CMake builds detect the common Snappy 1.3.1
package staged by the ordinary pkgsrc recipe; native write, read, compaction,
reopen and delete pass. Cache and Options headers are unchanged and their
native sizes match 1.23. Target execution, LevelDB package lifecycle and full
browser acceptance have not been tested.
